Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: discard delayed resampler samples on transform flush

A resampler holds audio history even when its format parameters are unchanged.
Flushing decoder and output queues while retaining that history lets samples
from before a seek appear in the next audio segment. Release the resampler on
explicit flush; convert_audio_frame already creates it lazily on the next frame.

Keep the negotiated output format and the established timestamp mapping from
0008. Leave the swscale parameter cache intact. This is a discard boundary,
not EOS or a format transition: those need separate tail-draining work, not
this reset. No change to continuous conversion or transform_drain.

The extracted SE1 methods reproduce old nonzero PCM after a flush into silence
with SE1's actual libswresample. This is not a Wine/VRChat playback result.
Independent proposal after SE1; do not change an already pinned candidate.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
@@ -1611,7 +1611,9 @@
     t->video_input_anchor_pts = INT64_MIN;
     t->video_pts_offset   = INT64_MIN;
     t->cumulative_samples = 0;
-    /* Don't free swr/sws — parameters haven't changed */
+    /* Discard delayed audio as well as decoded/output samples. The resampler
+     * is recreated on demand; the swscale parameter cache can be retained. */
+    swr_free( &t->swr );
     return STATUS_SUCCESS;
 }
 
